{"chunk_id": "7717440d1039", "text": "After days of relentless wrestling, Jarasandha finally shows signs of exhaustion on the fourteenth night. Krishna notices and advises Bhima to match the king\u2019s remaining strength rather than press a dying foe unfairly. Understanding the moment, Bhima resolves to end the duel. Encouraged by Krishna, he lifts Jarasandha, whirls him a hundred times, and breaks his body across his knee, killing the long\u2011unconquered ruler of Magadha. The thunderous roar of Bhima terrifies the city. Krishna, Bhima, and Arjuna then free the many kings whom Jarasandha had imprisoned. The rescued rulers honor Krishna and pledge support for Yudhishthira\u2019s planned Rajasuya sacrifice. The episode marks a decisive political turning point: with Jarasandha gone, the path opens for Yudhishthira to claim imperial sovereignty.\nBhima kills Jarasandha in combat; Krishna frees imprisoned kings and urges them to support Yudhishthira\u2019s Rajasuya sacrifice.\nThemes: heroic combat, tyrant\u2019s downfall, divine guidance, liberation of kings, imperial ambition", "vector": [-0.013169574551284313, -0.010449192486703396, 0.001366010750643909, 0.007402896881103516, -0.006917351856827736, 0.008087980560958385, -0.02136397548019886, -0.013202830217778683, -0.019501611590385437, -0.01634889468550682, 0.014366808347404003, 0.008620085194706917, 0.019834177568554878, 0.003091191640123725, -0.005962890572845936, 0.004699143581092358, 0.0444306842982769, 0.0008821286610327661, 0.028919853270053864, -0.023678628727793694, 0.010522357188165188, -0.02073875442147255, -0.004010734148323536, 0.020645635202527046, -0.029212510213255882, 0.03477299585938454, 0.014779188670217991, -0.02148369885981083, 0.002979782409965992, -0.005221270490437746, -0.010276258923113346, 0.0012188507243990898, -0.0021616725716739893, 0.01298998948186636, -0.023199735209345818, 0.012670726515352726, 0.008187750354409218, -0.014978727325797081, 0.006228942424058914, -0.01285031158477068, 0